#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059469 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/id #uuid "d2698dbf-dea6-5abb-970e-a3ace180e337" :question/math-academy-id "e-4341" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,-4,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -7,0,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 0)i-(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-7))j+(3\\cdot 0-(-4)\\cdot (-7))k \\\\  & =-8i-13j-28k \\\\  & =⟨-8,-13,-28⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059470 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/id #uuid "b834e666-de4f-5964-a280-6571ad44b6bd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4343" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3, 1, 2x \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,1,x \\rangle,$ and $|\\,\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\,| = \\sqrt{19}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2x \\\\ 0 & 1 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2x \\\\ 1 & x\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2x \\\\ 0 & x\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-xi-3xj+3k \\\\  & =⟨-x,-3x,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-x)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & |\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}+9=19 \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}=10 \\\\  & {x}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x= \\pm 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383111 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57953a7d-6ff5-5463-82b3-660a7987ac8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11i-j+5k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383113} {:answer/id #uuid "27c215c9-fe3c-5325-938d-c796e57eb634" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-29i+j-5k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383114} {:answer/id #uuid "061e74b8-3931-5289-87d9-9776b30ee217" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11i+11j+5k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383115} {:answer/id #uuid "dae7e813-707b-5c06-9e78-0d1480ffe79d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-29i-11j+5k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383116} {:answer/id #uuid "b1169631-86bb-5015-9196-dae826e69684" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-29i-j+11k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dae7e813-707b-5c06-9e78-0d1480ffe79d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-29i-11j+5k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383116} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ef9ec5b-393d-5964-a2c0-18d16c79f679" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f616f27-cbd2-5b9b-b7d3-d436fd70b303" :question/math-academy-id "q-1392" :question/problem "Let $a=2i-3j+5k$ and $b=-i+4j+3k.$ Determine $a\\times b.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-3\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 4)i-(2\\cdot 3-5\\cdot (-1))j+(2\\cdot 4-(-3)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =(-9-20)i-(6-(-5))j+(8-3)k \\\\  & =-29i-11j+5k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059968 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4099fc6-4419-5b7b-a905-a6c0a6e3d1d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-28,19,-19⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383119} {:answer/id #uuid "5f52439d-0c8a-563f-bfbf-553783de1c3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-28,-19,-61⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383120} {:answer/id #uuid "75196dde-d0e2-529f-83e4-c9364d5b43b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨28,-19,-19⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383121} {:answer/id #uuid "09e68857-5257-54a9-a3eb-cc41ba63683c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-18,19,-61⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383122} {:answer/id #uuid "88928849-69c7-52e5-8d1e-9fd1d9e7d64a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨18,19,61⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09e68857-5257-54a9-a3eb-cc41ba63683c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-18,19,-61⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383122} :answer-field/id #uuid "293f3c53-406e-5616-b697-b7073a605221" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383118}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7427d773-9726-5cf6-8261-06dbd4949f9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-1405" :question/problem "Let $u=⟨-3,10,4⟩$ and $v=⟨4,7,1⟩.$ Find $u\\times v.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 10 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}10 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 10 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(10\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 7)i-((-3)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 4)j+((-3)\\cdot 7-10\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =(10-28)i-(-3-16)j+(-21-40)k \\\\  & =-18i+19j-61k \\\\  & =⟨-18,19,-61⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383124 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c1d030a-8518-555d-87b8-86c851b3eb46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-92,-6,34⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383126} {:answer/id #uuid "94ff1415-cc32-5f53-8ed1-629e62d25b4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-101,6,-34⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383127} {:answer/id #uuid "713a2785-4724-5524-8d08-06189fa3d665" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-52,-6,-34⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383128} {:answer/id #uuid "b7c30b86-db55-5f2a-9146-4093dd8c9e2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-52,6,34⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383129} {:answer/id #uuid "e078cc04-bcc6-5d16-b701-0f9b9e1fe113" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-92,6,-34⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e078cc04-bcc6-5d16-b701-0f9b9e1fe113" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-92,6,-34⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383130} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a354acb-ef01-5618-a4e0-6ac9fd33bc6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383125}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dae45d75-d684-55e4-a0b1-226126494890" :question/math-academy-id "q-1409" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-3,5,9⟩$ and $b=⟨2,8,-4⟩.$ Find $a\\times b.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 9 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(5\\cdot (-4)-9\\cdot 8)i-((-3)\\cdot (-4)-9\\cdot 2)j+((-3)\\cdot 8-5\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =(-20-72)i-(12-18)j+(-24-10)k \\\\  & =-92i+6j-34k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383131 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2650d32-83d9-5be2-88fe-9082308d1040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-15,5,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383133} {:answer/id #uuid "f47c80f6-6be1-5ec3-b010-376ccff934ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-15,3,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383134} {:answer/id #uuid "a34b7c3a-3600-522e-854c-b0c1c11fcd32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,-15,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383135} {:answer/id #uuid "466663d6-a22f-53c9-b79f-a576f5bbc651" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨15,5,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383136} {:answer/id #uuid "681d4b47-85b1-53ce-9943-6c3fe26d1ac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,5,12⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f47c80f6-6be1-5ec3-b010-376ccff934ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-15,3,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383134} :answer-field/id #uuid "92f57354-3f7a-5d35-9ff6-e79d3895c8f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "765f0999-da93-5e44-b207-672576084830" :question/math-academy-id "q-19779" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨1,0,3⟩$ and $b=⟨2,5,3⟩.$ Find $a\\times b.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 3-3\\cdot 5)i-(1\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 3)j+(1\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =(0-15)i-(3-6)j+(5-0)k \\\\  & =⟨-15,3,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383138 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "527a9067-66e0-5541-8a31-09be2917738c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383140} {:answer/id #uuid "07e4a400-7efe-58db-bb86-a9f0506852ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383141} {:answer/id #uuid "3330120f-0c0d-5b50-8d19-4b55bd943eee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383142} {:answer/id #uuid "3faf4237-6786-52d7-9205-e0fd4294b6e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5,-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383143} {:answer/id #uuid "f5dcc2af-7c42-5941-ad40-c859d47a1c48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07e4a400-7efe-58db-bb86-a9f0506852ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383141} :answer-field/id #uuid "62f7e535-c409-5713-83d1-e12bd82fe322" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e49fd82-b772-500c-ae05-d9a02fdf2670" :question/math-academy-id "q-19785" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,2,3⟩$, $b=⟨2x,5,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{393}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2x & 5 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ 2x & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 2 \\\\ 2x & 5\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4-15)i-(2x-6x)j+(5x-4x)k \\\\  & =⟨-11,4x,x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-11)^{2}+(4x)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{121+16{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+121}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{393} \\\\ \\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+121} & =\\sqrt{393} \\\\ 17{x}^{2}+121 & =393 \\\\ 17{x}^{2} & =272 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b2e1274-8ce1-5f89-86a6-68c8a3a535ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b2e1274-8ce1-5f89-86a6-68c8a3a535ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383147} :answer-field/id #uuid "519f7793-f8c7-5470-b79e-2c47491b4f63" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d0d4f1f4-092c-54ed-bec7-e3d695b165da" :question/math-academy-id "q-278839" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,2,1⟩,$ $b=⟨2,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{20}.$ Find $x.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(x-2)j+(0-4)k \\\\  & =⟨2,2-x,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(2-x)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4-4x+{x}^{2}+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-4x+24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-4x+24} & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+24 & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+4 & =0 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383148 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62a1d2ea-4689-59bc-90dc-13d6d3b0f036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62a1d2ea-4689-59bc-90dc-13d6d3b0f036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383150} :answer-field/id #uuid "714ecb69-2242-5a62-a2dd-e0c62459d9d0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383149} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3499a533-1f1a-5f85-b65d-cdbd4fbf4ae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3499a533-1f1a-5f85-b65d-cdbd4fbf4ae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383152} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3d7fa9d-7890-5d84-9a7d-29012cad761f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383151} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0692546a-0c1d-54a4-8df4-1c427a28b486" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383154}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0692546a-0c1d-54a4-8df4-1c427a28b486" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383154} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2708ea4-ba98-5180-a886-9e3fb4dd53ed" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "218e8213-0786-589f-9101-a628c7485d08" :question/math-academy-id "q-281977" :question/problem "Let $u=⟨\\frac{2}{3},0,1⟩$ and $v=⟨1,2,-3⟩.$ Find $u\\times v.$\n\n$u\\times v=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((0)(-3)-(1)(2))i-((\\frac{2}{3})(-3)-(1)(1))j+((\\frac{2}{3})(2)-(0)(1))k \\\\  & =(0-2)i-(-2-1)j+(\\frac{4}{3})k \\\\  & =-2i+3j+(\\frac{4}{3})k \\\\  & =⟨-2,3,\\frac{4}{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383155 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6f989d7-af00-5d2f-a005-da257cbe76b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383157} {:answer/id #uuid "62a45098-3021-5e55-b988-085ae375d93e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6f989d7-af00-5d2f-a005-da257cbe76b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383157} :answer-field/id #uuid "256ebc4c-7f6c-5393-be95-9e64d9415fb7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383156} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22afe76c-d28e-5871-be02-a348baebd7b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22afe76c-d28e-5871-be02-a348baebd7b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383160} :answer-field/id #uuid "e881a6e8-a1d8-5d3d-81c9-8a43bf4cb1cb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69cd45e2-ef00-59cc-9c12-4889a1ef7992" :question/math-academy-id "q-282261" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,0,1⟩,$ $b=⟨-x,2,0⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{29}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 0 & 1 \\\\ -x & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ -x & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 0 \\\\ -x & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0-2)i-(0+x)j+(2x+0)k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-x,2x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-x)^{2}+(2x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+{x}^{2}+4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{x}^{2}+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{29} \\\\ \\sqrt{5{x}^{2}+4} & =\\sqrt{29} \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+4 & =29 \\\\ 5{x}^{2} & =25 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-\\sqrt{5},$ $x=\\sqrt{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dcb1cbd-94dd-5ec7-a370-51627c867ef2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7dcb1cbd-94dd-5ec7-a370-51627c867ef2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304181} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcb4ef77-6cb3-5d3f-b4c1-653cc0729217" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dee8668-d5bd-5bbb-8e15-abc9e8c4f1ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dee8668-d5bd-5bbb-8e15-abc9e8c4f1ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304183} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b2f2c49-3c37-5b34-953e-85c4bdac5471" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "077d8348-aacc-5cfe-9c4f-83cd2cce459b" :question/math-academy-id "q-282278" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨3,0,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{157}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(4x-12)j+(0-3)k \\\\  & =⟨2,12-4x,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(12-4x)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+(144-96x+16{x}^{2})+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-96x+157}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{157} \\\\ \\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-96x+157} & =\\sqrt{157} \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-96x+157 & =157 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-96x & =0 \\\\ 16x(x-6) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,x=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=0,$ $x=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75b4e25f-1030-5b07-89ea-2c0a3d618edc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304186} {:answer/id #uuid "67d14441-a0c9-5061-a93c-e5acee68411f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304187} {:answer/id #uuid "69682917-4196-5bce-8932-d2047ba4f27f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304188} {:answer/id #uuid "2cb2ab75-866a-5bcb-b308-7f16325a231f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304189} {:answer/id #uuid "e51be6ff-88ca-52a1-b0ad-255306fa8a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cb2ab75-866a-5bcb-b308-7f16325a231f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304189} :answer-field/id #uuid "87a9aae2-c040-564a-9d2d-e42640d1113c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54ac0cd9-756f-56ec-a02b-bc51faafb7b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-77427" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2,x,1⟩,$ $b=⟨1,-x,3⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=10.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & x & 1 \\\\ 1 & -x & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ -x & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & x \\\\ 1 & -x\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3x+x)i-(6-1)j+(-2x-x)k \\\\  & =⟨4x,-5,-3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+25+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25({x}^{2}+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =10 \\\\ \\sqrt{25({x}^{2}+1)} & =10 \\\\ 25({x}^{2}+1) & =100 \\\\ {x}^{2}+1 & =4 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}.$"}]}
